    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d366">

                <pb facs="0994" n="982" xml:id="pg982"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.50 UNRRA/5–2345</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of the British Embassy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Marris</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Acheson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">RS 10AM/93/45</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-23">May 23, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Dean</hi>: We have now had a reply from the
                    Foreign Office about the Yugoslav displaced persons problem.<anchor n="71"
                        xml:id="d366-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>I attach a copy of this telegram and I suggest, if this is agreeable to you, that
                    you should let me know how we both ought next to proceed.</p>
                <p>I fancy the Governor himself is away so, if this is so, perhaps we ought to talk
                    to Hendrickson.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Denny Marris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d366-a1.xml" xpointer="d366-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d366-f1" n="71" xml:id="d366-f1-content">
                <p>UNRRA was exploring with the Department of State and the British Embassy possible
                    solutions to the problem of displaced Yugoslavs (840.50 UNRRA/5–1945).</p>
                <p>For documentation on the overall question of displaced persons and refugees, see
                        <ref target="#pg1146">pp. 1146</ref> ff.; see also <ref
                        target="frus1945Berlinv01#pg_1064">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Conference of Berlin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Potsdam</hi>), vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, Index, p.
                        1064</ref>, and <ref target="frus1945Berlinv02#pg_1611">vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, Index, p. 1611</ref>. For UNRRA’s role
                    in general displaced persons operations, see Woodbridge, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >UNRRA</hi>, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, pp. 469 ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
